#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.43 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:5
msgid "Backward Compatibility Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:12
msgid ""
"The \"--rfc\" option of \"git format-patch\" used to be a valid way to "
"override an earlier \"--subject-prefix=<something>\" on the command line and "
"replace it with \"[RFC PATCH]\", but from this release, it merely prefixes "
"the string \"RFC \" in front of the given subject prefix.  If you are "
"negatively affected by this change, please use \"--subject-prefix=PATCH "
"--rfc\" as a replacement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:21
msgid ""
"In Git 2.42, \"git rev-list --stdin\" learned to take non-revisions (like "
"\"--not\") from the standard input, but the way such a \"--not\" was handled "
"was quite confusing, which has been rethought.  The updated rule is that "
"\"--not\" given from the command line only affects revs given from the "
"command line that comes but not revs read from the standard input, and "
"\"--not\" read from the standard input affects revs given from the standard "
"input and not revs given from the command line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:23
msgid "UI, Workflows & Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:30
msgid ""
"A message written in olden time prevented a branch from getting checked out, "
"saying it is already checked out elsewhere. But these days, we treat a "
"branch that is being bisected or rebased just like a branch that is checked "
"out and protect it from getting modified with the same codepath.  The "
"message has been rephrased to say that the branch is \"in use\" to avoid "
"confusion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:33
msgid ""
"Hourly and other schedules of \"git maintenance\" jobs are randomly "
"distributed now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:36
msgid ""
"\"git cmd -h\" learned to signal which options can be negated by listing "
"such options like \"--[no-]opt\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:40
msgid ""
"The way authentication related data other than passwords (e.g., oauth token "
"and password expiration data) are stored in libsecret keyrings has been "
"rethought."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:44
msgid ""
"Update the libsecret and wincred credential helpers to correctly match which "
"credential to erase; they erased the wrong entry in some cases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:46
msgid "Git GUI updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:51
msgid ""
"\"git format-patch\" learned a new \"--description-file\" option that lets "
"cover letter description to be fed; this can be used on detached HEAD where "
"there is no branch description available, and also can override the branch "
"description if there is one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:55
msgid ""
"Use of the \"--max-pack-size\" option to allow multiple packfiles to be "
"created is now supported even when we are sending unreachable objects to "
"cruft packs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:59
msgid ""
"\"git format-patch --rfc --subject-prefix=<foo>\" used to ignore the "
"\"--subject-prefix\" option and used \"[RFC PATCH]\"; now we will add "
"\"RFC\" prefix to whatever subject prefix is specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:62
msgid ""
"\"git log --format\" has been taught the %(decorate) placeholder for further "
"customization over what the \"--decorate\" option offers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:67
msgid ""
"The default log message created by \"git revert\", when reverting a commit "
"that records a revert, has been tweaked, to encourage people to describe "
"complex \"revert of revert of revert\" situations better in their own words."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:70
msgid ""
"The command-line completion support (in contrib/) learned to complete \"git "
"commit --trailer=\" for possible trailer keys."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:73
msgid ""
"\"git update-index\" learned the \"--show-index-version\" option to inspect "
"the index format version used by the on-disk index file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:76
msgid ""
"\"git diff\" learned the \"diff.statNameWidth\" configuration variable, to "
"give the default width for the name part in the \"--stat\" output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:80
msgid ""
"\"git range-diff --notes=foo\" compared \"log --notes=foo --notes\" of the "
"two ranges, instead of using just the specified notes tree, which has been "
"corrected to use only the specified notes tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:86
msgid ""
"The command line completion script (in contrib/) can be told to complete "
"aliases by including \": git <cmd> ;\" in the alias to tell it that the "
"alias should be completed in a similar way to how \"git <cmd>\" is "
"completed.  The parsing code for the alias has been loosened to allow ';' "
"without an extra space before it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:91
msgid ""
"\"git for-each-ref\" and friends learned to apply mailmap to authorname and "
"other fields in a more flexible way than using separate placeholder letters "
"like %a[eElL] every time we want to come up with small variants."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:94
msgid ""
"\"git repack\" machinery learned to pay attention to the \"--filter=\" "
"option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:97
msgid ""
"\"git repack\" learned the \"--max-cruft-size\" option to prevent cruft "
"packs from growing without bounds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:100
msgid ""
"\"git merge-tree\" learned to take strategy backend specific options via the "
"\"-X\" option, like \"git merge\" does."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:103
msgid ""
"\"git log\" and friends learned the \"--dd\" option that is a short-hand for "
"\"--diff-merges=first-parent -p\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:107
msgid ""
"The attribute subsystem learned to honor the \"attr.tree\" configuration "
"variable that specifies which tree to read the .gitattributes files from."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:110
msgid ""
"\"git merge-file\" learns a mode to read three variants of the contents to "
"be merged from blob objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:113
msgid "Performance, Internal Implementation, Development Support etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:115
msgid "\"git check-attr\" has been taught to work better with sparse-index."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:120
msgid ""
"It may be tempting to leave the help text NULL for a command line option "
"that is either hidden or too obvious, but \"git subcmd -h\" and \"git subcmd "
"--help-all\" would have segfaulted if done so.  Now the help text is truly "
"optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:122
msgid "Tests that are known to pass with LSan are now marked as such."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:125
msgid ""
"Flaky \"git p4\" tests, as well as \"git svn\" tests, are now skipped in the "
"(rather expensive) sanitizer CI job."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:129
msgid ""
"Tests with LSan from time to time seem to emit harmless messages that make "
"our tests unnecessarily flaky; we work around it by filtering the "
"uninteresting output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:132
msgid ""
"Unused parameters to functions are marked as such, and/or removed, in order "
"to bring us closer to \"-Wunused-parameter\" clean."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:135
msgid ""
"The code to keep track of existing packs in the repository while repacking "
"has been refactored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:139
msgid ""
"The \"streaming\" interface used for bulk-checkin codepath has been narrowed "
"to take only blob objects for now, with no real loss of functionality."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:141
msgid "GitHub CI workflow has learned to trigger Coverity check."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:143
msgid "Test coverage for trailers has been improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:146
msgid ""
"The code to iterate over loose references has been optimized to reduce the "
"number of lstat() system calls."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:149
msgid ""
"The codepaths that read \"chunk\" formatted files have been corrected to pay "
"attention to the chunk size and notice broken files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:152
msgid ""
"Replace macos-12 used at GitHub CI with macos-13.  (merge 682a868f67 "
"js/ci-use-macos-13 later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.42"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:159
msgid ""
"Overly long label names used in the sequencer machinery are now chopped to "
"fit under filesystem limitation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:161
msgid "Scalar updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:165
msgid ""
"Tweak GitHub Actions CI so that pushing the same commit to multiple branch "
"tips at the same time will not waste building and testing the same thing "
"twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:168
msgid ""
"The commit-graph verification code that detects a mixture of zero and "
"non-zero generation numbers has been updated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:171
msgid ""
"\"git diff -w --exit-code\" with various options did not work correctly, "
"which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:176
msgid ""
"The \"transfer.unpackLimit\" configuration variable ought to be used as a "
"fallback, but overrode the more specific \"fetch.unpackLimit\" and "
"\"receive.unpackLimit\" configuration variables by mistake, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:179
msgid ""
"The use of API between two calls to require_clean_work_tree() from the "
"sequencer code has been cleaned up for consistency."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:182
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-such-option\" and other corner cases around the exit status "
"of the \"diff\" command have been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:185
msgid ""
"\"git for-each-ref --sort='contents:size'\" sorted the refs according to "
"size numerically, giving a ref that points at a blob twelve-byte"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:186
msgid "long before showing a blob hundred-byte (100) long, which has"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:187
msgid "been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:191
msgid ""
"We now limit the depth of the tree objects and maximum length of pathnames "
"recorded in tree objects.  (merge 4d5693ba05 jk/tree-name-and-depth-limit "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:194
msgid ""
"Various fixes to the behavior of \"rebase -i\", when the command got "
"interrupted by conflicting changes, have been made."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:197
msgid ""
"References from a description of the `--patch` option in various manual "
"pages have been simplified and improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:200
msgid ""
"\"git grep -e A --no-or -e B\" is accepted, even though the negation of the "
"\"--or\" option did not mean anything, which has been tightened."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:204
msgid ""
"The completion script (in contrib/) has been taught to treat the \"-t\" "
"option to \"git checkout\" and \"git switch\" just like the \"--track\" "
"option, to complete remote-tracking branches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:207
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-index -R <(one) <(two)\" did not work correctly, which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:210
msgid ""
"\"git maintenance\" timers' implementation has been updated, based on "
"systemd timers, to work with WSL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:214
msgid ""
"\"git diff --cached\" codepath did not fill the necessary stat information "
"for a file when fsmonitor knows it is clean and ended up behaving as if it "
"were not clean, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:219
msgid ""
"How \"alias.foo = : git cmd ; aliased-command-string\" should be spelled "
"with necessary whitespace around punctuation marks to work has been more "
"clearly documented (but this will be moot with newer versions of Git where "
"the parsing rules have been improved)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:223
msgid ""
"HTTP Header redaction code has been adjusted for a newer version of cURL "
"library that shows its traces differently from earlier versions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:226
msgid ""
"An error message given by \"git send-email\", when given a malformed "
"address, did not show the offending address, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:229
msgid ""
"UBSan options were not propagated through the test framework to git run via "
"the httpd, unlike ASan options, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:234
msgid ""
"\"checkout --merge -- path\" and \"update-index --unresolve path\" did not "
"resurrect conflicted state that was resolved to remove path, but now they "
"do.  (merge 5bdedac3c7 jc/unresolve-removal later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:238
msgid ""
"The display width table for unicode characters has been updated for Unicode "
"15.1 (merge 872976c37e bb/unicode-width-table-15 later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:241
msgid ""
"Update mailmap entry for Derrick.  (merge 6e5457d8c7 ds/mailmap-entry-update "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:250
msgid ""
"In the \".gitmodules\" files, submodules are keyed by their names, and the "
"path to the submodule whose name is $name is specified by the "
"submodule.$name.path variable.  There were a few codepaths that mixed the "
"name and path up when consulting the submodule database, which have been "
"corrected.  It took long for these bugs to be found as the name of a "
"submodule initially is the same as its path, and the problem does not "
"surface until it is moved to a different path, which apparently happens very "
"rarely."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:256
msgid ""
"\"git diff --merge-base X other args...\" insisted that X must be a commit "
"and errored out when given an annotated tag that peels to a commit, but we "
"only need it to be a committish.  This has been corrected.  (merge "
"4adceb5a29 ar/diff-index-merge-base-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:260
msgid ""
"\"git merge-tree\" used to segfault when the \"--attr-source\" option is "
"used, which has been corrected.  (merge e95bafc52f "
"jc/merge-ort-attr-index-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:264
msgid ""
"Unlike \"git log --pretty=%D\", \"git log --pretty=\"%(decorate)\" did not "
"auto-initialize the decoration subsystem, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:268
msgid ""
"Feeding \"git stash store\" with a random commit that was not created by "
"\"git stash create\" now errors out.  (merge d9b6634589 "
"jc/fail-stash-to-store-non-stash later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:275
msgid ""
"The index file has room only for the lower 32-bit of the file size in the "
"cached stat information, which means cached stat information will have 0 in "
"its sd_size member for a file whose size is a multiple of 4GiB.  This is "
"mistaken for a racily clean path.  Avoid it by storing a bogus sd_size value "
"instead for such files.  (merge 5143ac07b1 bc/racy-4gb-files later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:279
msgid ""
"\"git p4\" tried to store symlinks to LFS when told, but has been fixed not "
"to do so, because it does not make sense.  (merge 10c89a02b0 "
"mm/p4-symlink-with-lfs later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:284
msgid ""
"The codepath to handle recipient addresses `git send-email --compose` learns "
"from the user was completely broken, which has been corrected.  (merge "
"3ec6167567 jk/send-email-fix-addresses-from-composed-messages later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:288
msgid ""
"\"cd sub && git grep -f patterns\" tried to read \"patterns\" file at the "
"top level of the working tree; it has been corrected to read "
"\"sub/patterns\" instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:291
msgid ""
"\"git reflog expire --single-worktree\" has been broken for the past 20 "
"months or so, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:295
msgid ""
"\"git send-email\" did not have certain pieces of data computed yet when it "
"tried to validate the outgoing messages and its recipient addresses, which "
"has been sorted out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:298
msgid ""
"\"git bugreport\" learned to complain when it received a command line "
"argument that it will not use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:304
msgid ""
"The codepath to traverse the commit-graph learned to notice that a commit is "
"missing (e.g., corrupt repository lost an object), even though it knows "
"something about the commit (like its parents) from what is in commit-graph.  "
"(merge 7a5d604443 ps/do-not-trust-commit-graph-blindly-for-existence later "
"to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:307
msgid ""
"\"git rev-list --missing\" did not work for missing commit objects, which "
"has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:311
msgid ""
"\"git rev-list --unpacked --objects\" failed to exclude packed non-commit "
"objects, which has been corrected.  (merge 7b3c8e9f38 "
"tb/rev-list-unpacked-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:315
msgid ""
"\"To dereference\" and \"to peel\" were sometimes used in in-code comments "
"and documentation but without description in the glossary.  (merge "
"893dce2ffb vd/glossary-dereference-peel later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.43.0.txt:323
msgid ""
"Other code cleanup, docfix, build fix, etc.  (merge c2c349a15c "
"xz/commit-title-soft-limit-doc later to maint).  (merge 1bd809938a "
"tb/format-pack-doc-update later to maint).  (merge 8f81532599 "
"an/clang-format-typofix later to maint).  (merge 3ca86adc2d "
"la/strvec-header-fix later to maint).  (merge 6789275d37 jc/test-i18ngrep "
"later to maint).  (merge 9972cd6004 ps/leakfixes later to maint).  (merge "
"46edab516b tz/send-email-helpfix later to maint)."
msgstr ""
